# What must never enter the console's build context.
#
# THIS FILE IS NOT OPTIONAL AND THE ROOT .dockerignore DOES NOT COVER IT.
# `compose.yaml` builds this image with `context: ./web`, and Docker resolves
# `.dockerignore` relative to the CONTEXT, not the repository. Without this
# file the context is `node_modules` plus `.next` -- measured at 300 MB and
# still climbing when it was first tried, several minutes of transfer before a
# single instruction ran, to ship files the build then throws away.
#
# Everything the image needs is either reinstalled from the lockfile (stage 1)
# or produced by `next build` (stage 2). Nothing excluded here is missed.

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.env.local` holds NEXT_PUBLIC_* overrides on a developer machine. Those are
# BUILD-TIME values, so a stray copy in the context would silently outrank the
# build args `compose.yaml` passes -- and the way that failure presents is a
# console serving mocks, which looks like a working demo.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- reinstalled, never copied ------------------------------------------------
node_modules

# --- rebuilt, never copied ----------------------------------------------------
.next
out
build
dist
next-env.d.ts

# --- irrelevant to a production build -----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
coverage
.vercel
